    "Normalisation bases differ in kind: the measurement uses the wind-tunnel approach flow at the model position (AF at z = 0.1D), the CFD uses the inlet log law at 1.5 m (5H upstream of the array, before the profile develops over the rough ground); with this run the inlet value is 4.5 % below AF(0.1D), so normalising the CFD by the AF value instead would lower every cfd_ratio by the same 4.5 % and raise FB. An upstream probe or an empty-domain run would give a second reference.",
